# hunt's secrets: copy to .secrets. KEY=value, one a line; leave a secret
# out rather than empty.

# hunt's owner, who signs in at /login and runs it. Without these: made in
# hunt's launcher, the first time it's opened. Set again, the password
# replaces theirs: the way back in when it's forgotten.
# HUNT_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
# HUNT_ADMIN_PASSWORD=a long passphrase

# PostgreSQL or MySQL instead of SQLite in the volume.
# HUNT_DB=postgres://hunt:secret@db.example.internal/hunt
